#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:4
msgid ""
"**Before creating any file**, check whether the user is working in a sub-"
"folder workspace. If so, preserve that workspace's `subproject:` "
"frontmatter and write the spec under the workspace's `.hero/` root; "
"otherwise write under the project `.hero/` root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:6
msgid ""
"**Stamp the active domain in frontmatter.** New bug specs MUST emit a "
"`domain:` field reflecting the workspace's active domain — run `hero "
"domain` (or read the `domain` key from `.hero/hero.json`; empty means "
"engineering) and write that value. This keeps bug specs under the correct"
" DSKG namespace partition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:8
msgid "Route this bug investigation to the `debug-investigator` agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:10
msgid ""
"Pass the bug report and any spec path or tracker ID to the agent. The "
"`debug-investigator` handles the complete diagnosis workflow: pre-flight "
"status check, investigation, root cause classification, fix planning, "
"spec writing, and tracker posting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:12
msgid ""
"**Before starting work**, emit `hero next ask` to capture the bug report "
"the user pasted in. This preserves session intent across compaction — see"
" the `next-handoff-emit` skill for the full pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:16
msgid ""
"**The agent must write all findings into the spec file on disk.** The "
"spec file is the deliverable, not chat output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:18
msgid ""
"**Always include a `## Kickoff` section** in the fix spec. Follow the "
"`kickoff-prompt` skill — the kickoff is a paste-ready cold-start prompt "
"for picking the fix work back up in a fresh session. Skipping it excludes"
" the spec from `hero queue` and triggers a `hero check` advisory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:20
msgid ""
"**After writing the fix spec, run `hero index --if-stale -q`** so it "
"surfaces in `hero search` / `hero list` / MCP tools without anyone "
"needing to run a manual reindex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:22
msgid ""
"**Before proposing a fix direction**, call `hero_anchor` to check project"
" tripwires. If any proposed fix would reintroduce a forbidden dependency,"
" pattern, or tool, eliminate that direction and find an alternative "
"within project constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:24
msgid ""
"If the `debug-investigator` returns with `Needs more research? → Yes`, "
"that is an acceptable outcome — report it to the user and move on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:28
msgid "Batch Mode: Diagnosing Multiple Bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:30
msgid ""
"When asked to diagnose multiple bugs (e.g. \"diagnose 10 bugs\", \"work "
"through the imported bugs\"):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:32
msgid ""
"**Always select from locally imported specs.** Run `hero search --list "
"--type bug` to see what's available. Apply filters like `--status "
"planning` or `--since YYYY-MM-DD` to narrow the list. **Never query the "
"tracker to pick work items.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:33
msgid ""
"**Filter out closed/completed specs.** Only select specs with an open "
"status (`planning`, `draft`, `active`). Skip anything marked `completed` "
"or `superseded`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:34
msgid ""
"**Present the selection to the user** before starting work. Show the list"
" of bugs you plan to diagnose and get confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:35
msgid ""
"**Default: one at a time.** Run each bug through the `debug-investigator`"
" agent sequentially. Complete the full diagnosis for one bug — including "
"writing the spec AND posting to the tracker (Step 8 of the agent) — "
"before moving to the next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:37
msgid "Parallel batch mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:39
msgid ""
"If the user explicitly asks to run diagnoses in parallel (e.g. \"run each"
" in an agent\", \"diagnose all of them at once\"), launch multiple Task "
"agents. **Each agent must follow these rules:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:41
msgid ""
"**Each agent runs as the `debug-investigator`**. Tell each agent: \"You "
"are the `debug-investigator`. Load the `debugging-investigation` skill. "
"Diagnose the bug described in the spec at `<spec-path>`. Write all "
"findings into the spec file on disk. After writing the spec, post results"
" to the tracker (see step 6).\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:42
msgid ""
"**Include the bug context** in each agent's prompt — the spec path, the "
"tracker ID, and a brief description of the bug. The agent will read the "
"full spec and any tracker issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:43
msgid ""
"**Each agent MUST write findings to its spec file on disk.** The spec "
"file is the deliverable. If the agent only reports findings in its "
"response without updating the spec file, the diagnosis is incomplete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:44
msgid ""
"**File safety: never delete, move, or rename spec files.** Each agent "
"works only on its assigned spec. Do not run `hero spec complete`, do not "
"move files between directories. The only file operation allowed is "
"editing the assigned spec in-place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:45
msgid ""
"**No cross-agent file access.** Each agent reads and writes only its own "
"assigned spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:46
msgid ""
"**Each agent MUST post to the tracker.** If the spec has a `tracker_id` "
"and a tracker is configured, the agent must run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:47
msgid ""
"`hero sync attach <tracker_id> <spec-path> <tracker_id>-diagnosis.md` to "
"upload the diagnosis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:48
msgid ""
"`hero sync comment <tracker_id> \"<summary>\"` to post a brief summary "
"(root cause, fix location, severity) If the agent skips this step, the "
"diagnosis is incomplete even if the spec file was written."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:51
msgid "After all agents complete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:53
msgid "Review the results:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:54
msgid ""
"For each bug, verify the spec file still exists on disk and contains "
"investigation findings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:55
msgid ""
"For each bug with a `tracker_id`, verify the agent posted to the tracker "
"(check its output for \"Comment posted\" / \"File attached\" "
"confirmation). Re-run any that missed the posting step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/diagnose.md:56
msgid ""
"Report any agents that failed to write to their spec file or post to "
"tracker — re-run those individually"
msgstr ""

